# The scheduled reports, run by the bot (bot.py). Same time syntax as crontab(5): minute hour day-of-month month
# day-of-week, or an @macro such as @daily. The command is a finbot script and its arguments; separate several with ";"
# to run them in turn.
# Times are in the server's own time zone, like cron; add a line "CRON_TZ=Australia/Melbourne" above a job to pin one.
# To change the schedule, copy this file to the data directory (util/sync_defaults.py --apply), edit the copy, then:
#   systemctl reload finbot

# Every 20 minutes on weekdays
*/20 * * * Mon-Fri trades.py

# Mid-session
00 01 * * Mon-Fri price.py midsession # AU
15 17 * * Mon-Fri price.py midsession # US

# Daily
30  21 * * * reminder.py

# Daily on weekdays
29  21 * * Mon-Fri price.py interday
10  11 * * Mon-Fri price.py premarket

# Weekly
28  21 * * Sat cal.py earnings; cal.py ex-dividend; price.py 7; performance.py 7; rating.py

# Housekeeping: delete cache files older than 30 days
51  18 * * Sat cleanup.py 30

# Monthly
27  21 1 * * shorts.py; price.py 28; performance.py 28


